config BR2_PACKAGE_CAM_GRAB
	bool "cam-grab"
	help
	  Small V4L2 camera capture tool for the msm8953 CAMSS pipeline
	  on the Fairphone 3+.

	  The CAMSS RDI lane only emits MIPI 10-bit packed Bayer (fourcc
	  `pgAA` / V4L2_PIX_FMT_SGRBG10P). GStreamer 1.24's v4l2src has
	  no mapping for this format and its `bayer2rgbneon` plugin only
	  consumes unpacked Bayer (`*10le`). cam-grab opens the V4L2
	  multi-planar device, captures frames, unpacks each 5-byte
	  group (4 packed 10-bit pixels) into 4 16-bit little-endian
	  values, and writes the result to stdout in `video/x-bayer,
	  format=grbg10le` byte order — ready to pipe into a GStreamer
	  pipeline via `fdsrc fd=0`.
